  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "6.0.2\n- Bundled Scriban's complete netstandard2.0 dependency chain, fixing CS8785 failures caused by missing System.Text.Json 10.0.0.0 in .NET SDK 9 compiler hosts.\n- Supplied the same private dependencies for NuGet consumption and analyzer project references, preserving JSON template functions without adding dependencies to consuming projects.\n- Retained Roslyn 4.3.1 compiler compatibility, settings version 6 and template compatibility version 6.0.\n\n6.0.1\n- Aligned with the Visual Studio extension patch that fixes settings and default-template migration when opening solutions configured for version 0.5.\n- Retained Roslyn 4.3.1 compiler compatibility, unchanged generated APIs, settings version 6 and template compatibility version 6.0.\n\n6.0.0\n- Adopted three-part release versions, with settings version 6 and template compatibility version 6.0.\n- Preserved generated Builder and FluentMock APIs; configuration migration is performed by the matching Visual Studio extension or MCP server.\n- Lowered the Roslyn API dependency to 4.3.1 so generators load in compiler hosts running Roslyn 4.3.1 or newer, including Roslyn 4.13.0 build agents.\n- Fixed missing BuilderForAttribute and FluentMockForAttribute errors caused by older compiler hosts rejecting the generator.\n\n0.5.3.2\n- Made Roslyn a private build-time dependency so compiler packages and their System.* dependencies do not flow into consumer projects or cause NU1605 package downgrades.\n- Ensured the package includes its shared domain assembly when built outside a solution.\n\n0.5.3\n- Corrected FluentMock generation for inherited and hidden members, including properties declared with new and namespace-qualified method types.\n- Corrected tuple type rendering in generated builder and FluentMock signatures.\n- Updated Scriban to 7.5.0 to address dependency security advisories.\n\n0.5.2\n- Added default settings when .easyTdd is absent.\n- Fixed builder and FluentMock generation for inherited members, hidden properties, and indexers.\n\n0.5.0.4\n- Excluded properties without public setters from builder generation.\n\n0.5.0.3\n- Prevented duplicate generation of overridden members in builders and tests.\n\n0.5.0.1\n- Maintained backward compatibility with version 0.4.0.5.\n\n0.5.0.0\n- Added the incremental FluentMock source generator.\n\n0.4.0.5\n- Fixed builder generation for same-named classes in different namespaces.\n\n0.4.0.3\n- Fixed template resolution when a template in the root .easyTdd directory shares a name with one in a subdirectory.\n\n0.4.0.0\n- Introduced the incremental builder source generator, with version numbering aligned to the EasyTdd Visual Studio extension.",
